                                                                    "patching_rect": [ 517.0, 260.0, 163.0, 275.0 ],
                                                                    "text": "to keep track of note-offs:\n\nnote-ons (note number+channel) stores corresponding event and chord note indices in a collection [coll]. a matching note-off (same note number and channel) causes the indices (event and chord note index) to be timestamped and stored to the event as an offset and then the note on is removed from the collection of held notes.\n\nrec off dumps any remaining notes in case they have not received any note-offs yet"
